{"author":{"id":"a3a282966ced55effb4560271fcd98e13241af24ea76b00ec76a0f18154bc8ee"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1790024818,"nonce":"DsNz5mQETlWQd6MLgy2yJJwiToc=","message":"From the config entity design (doc/design/config-entity.md, 3556569): relation types are leaves relations/\u003ckey\u003e = {name, inverse, cardinality: one|many}. One leaf declares both directions: inverse is only the name the derived side reads as (parent -\u003e child, blocks -\u003e blocked-by), never a key an issue can write, matching D4's 'store one side, derive the inverse'. Write-time validation checks inverse names are unique and collide with no key (E6). The cache's reverse index reads these types from RepoCache.Schema().","files":null}]}